          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use plant protein powder in baking?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, and it often bakes moister than whey because pea and rice proteins absorb more liquid. Expect a denser crumb and an earthy note, which suits banana bread, chocolate and spice recipes. Add more liquid than you would for whey, and let the batter rest before baking so it fully hydrates."
